{%- comment -%}
  The file table: files directly in the directory, then its subdirectories.
  Included by subgraph.liquid; reads `files`, `subdirs`, `folded` and
  `summary`.

  A subdirectory row says WHAT IT IS (subdir-what.liquid): declared by the
  caller when it resolved a description, else read from the subdirectory
  itself — its README, a self-describing file, or the kinds of file it holds.
  It never prints a file count (bean `ba9e`). A count drifts on every commit
  that adds a file: one line of `beans/README.md` conflicted three times in a
  single day (2026-10-01), and 207 such counts in 54 READMEs made almost every
  merge conflict. The numbers are in the writer's `Plan.counts`, for a
  harness to publish where they cannot conflict.

  Over the subdirectory limit (`folded`), the subdirectory rows move into a
  `<details>` disclosure after the file table, every row still there. The
  `markdown="1"` attribute is what makes kramdown (Jekyll, the github-pages
  build) read the table inside as markdown; GitHub reads it regardless, given
  the blank lines around it.

  The table is written only when it has a row. Over the list limit `files` is
  empty, and with no subdirectory either the summary is the whole answer: a
  header and separator with no body is not a table to kramdown, which keeps
  it as a paragraph and turns `---` into an em dash.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if summary != "" -%}
_{{ summary }}_

{% endif -%}
{%- if files.size == 0 and subdirs.size == 0 -%}
{%- if summary == "" -%}
_This directory holds no files yet._
{%- endif -%}
{%- elsif folded -%}
{%- if files.size > 0 -%}
| file | what it is | used by |
|---|---|---|
{% for f in files -%}
| [`{{ f.path }}`]({{ f.href }}) | {{ f.what }} | {{ f.usedBy }} |
{% endfor %}
{% endif -%}
<details markdown="1">
<summary>Subdirectories, by name — expand to list them</summary>

| subdirectory | what it is |
|---|---|
{% for d in subdirs -%}
| [`{{ d.name }}/`]({% if d.readme != "" %}{{ d.readme }}{% else %}{{ d.href }}/{% endif %}) | {% include subdir-what.liquid d=d %} |
{% endfor %}
</details>
{%- else -%}
| file | what it is | used by |
|---|---|---|
{% for f in files -%}
| [`{{ f.path }}`]({{ f.href }}) | {{ f.what }} | {{ f.usedBy }} |
{% endfor -%}
{% for d in subdirs -%}
| [`{{ d.name }}/`]({% if d.readme != "" %}{{ d.readme }}{% else %}{{ d.href }}/{% endif %}) | {% include subdir-what.liquid d=d %} | |
{% endfor -%}
{%- endif %}
